=== 2026-10-31 · motion-and-sound-designer · Local Hisham-clone narration of every spoken sound (in progress, part 0: plan) ===
Lead / asked by: lead agent, relaying owner Hisham 2026-10-31 "let's use local cloned voice arabic Hisham to record all sounds for better quality"
Files reviewed: BRIEF.md, ~/Work/Whisper-audio/bakeoff/narrate.py + qa_norm.py, assets/kids.js (speak, clipFor, WORD_CLIPS, LABELS, grownup card), lessons/{article,story,presentation}.html, games/write.js + strokes.json, mockups/*, guide.html
Decisions / judgement calls:
  - [NARRATION] Owner decision supersedes the house rule "local model English only, never Arabic" and the ElevenLabs recipe for this job — why: explicit owner request; risk (softened ق ص ط ض) handled by Whisper QA + listing every failed clip for an ear check.
  - [NARRATION] Driver = my own script in the session scratchpad that imports narrate.py (Narrator, score, BREAK_RE) and overrides best_take with a stricter Fusha check; narrate.py itself NOT modified — why: deck mode stops at the first lax "ok", and for <=6-word refs score() accepts any 1-word miss, so a single word could pass even when wrong.
  - [AUDIO-QA] Fusha strict pass = score ok AND cer <= 0.12 AND no softened emphatic AND no Egyptian-ism (ق→ء/ا, ث→ت/س, ذ→ز/د) in Whisper's text. Egyptian = narrate.py criteria.
  - [AUDIO-QA] Output: trim edge silence, two-pass loudnorm I=-16 LUFS TP=-1.5, mono 44.1 kHz 64 kbps mp3.
  - [SFX] Spoken via KS.speak: data-say (41 unique), morph pairs (4 new), quiz say (6 words + 2 questions + «هَذِهِ بِنْتٌ…»), story find-it line, write game (12 item names, 37 steps, 5 hints, 3 status lines). write.js prefix+number goes to #stepNo only, never spoken — no number variants needed. Classroom deck plays audio/samples/ar/s1–s3 (part 4). Web book uses page clips only.
  - [SFX] Key scheme: kids.js clipFor maps bare(text) → LABELS name only, so phrases have no key yet. Picture words keep LABELS names (cat, cat-f…); phrases/instructions get readable slugs; I hand the lead a bare-text→key map literal.
[GPU] pgrep empty at start.
  [MAJOR] [GPU] 2026-10-31 I started a 3-clip test run (≈70 s) while a draw-things-cli batch from ~/Work/AI_server (logo concepts) was running — my pgrep printed it but the same shell line went on. No crash. Fix: every run now goes through a guard that refuses to start if pgrep finds anything; waiting for Draw Things to stay idle 2 min before any further run.
  [AUDIO-QA] test: «قِطَّةٌ» alone → 5/5 takes garbage (0.4–0.5 s; heard «ريت», «تتتت»); «هَذَا قِطٌّ» softened ق→ك in 4/5 takes, take 5 clean; the 9-word find-it line passed first take. Lone words are the hard case.
